{"document":{"type":"root","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your long tool holds the HTTP call until the work ends. You have no task id for the host to poll."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Set "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execution: 'task'"},{"type":"text","value":" on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"toolDefinition"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The handler returns a task handle before the work ends. The tool function continues in this process. There is no queue."}]},{"type":"code","value":"import { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer, inMemoryTaskStore } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst taskStore = inMemoryTaskStore()\n\nconst buildReport = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'build_report',\n  description: 'Build a long report',\n  execution: 'task',\n}).server(async () => {\n  const text = await writeReport()\n  return { text }\n})\n\nasync function writeReport() {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 5000)\n  })\n  return 'Quarterly report'\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(\n    request: Request,\n    _env: unknown,\n    ctx: { waitUntil(promise: Promise<unknown>): void },\n  ) {\n    const server = createMCPServer({\n      name: 'reports',\n      version: '1.0.0',\n      tools: [buildReport],\n      taskStore,\n      waitUntil: (promise) => ctx.waitUntil(promise),\n    })\n    return server.fetch(request)\n  },\n}","lang":"ts"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Your tool function returns the final value. When the tool function ends, the store saves that value."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"what-a-task-tool-can-use","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What a task tool can use"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The task keeps running after the call returns the task handle. So the task does not use the request that started it."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.requestInput"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an error. Ask for input in a tool without "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execution: 'task'"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" calls the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":" option of "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createMCPServer"},{"type":"text","value":". If you do not pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sample"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.context.sample"},{"type":"text","value":" throws an error."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ctx.abortSignal"},{"type":"text","value":" does not abort when the call request ends."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-the-worker-alive","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the Worker alive"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you run on a Worker, pass "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitUntil"},{"type":"text","value":" from the Worker context."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The server calls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitUntil"},{"type":"text","value":" with the tool promise. After the store saves the tool result or the tool error, this promise settles."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If you omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitUntil"},{"type":"text","value":", a Worker can stop before the tool function ends. On one long-lived process, you can omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"waitUntil"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"keep-the-task-record","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Keep the task record"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":true,"start":1,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Create the store with "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemoryTaskStore"},{"type":"text","value":" outside "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"fetch"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Pass this store as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taskStore"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A new store on each request has no record of the old task."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The package "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"@tanstack/ai-mcp/server"},{"type":"text","value":" exports "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"inMemoryTaskStore"},{"type":"text","value":". The default store keeps each task in memory for this process. If you build the server once, you can omit "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taskStore"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If more than one instance can receive "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/get"},{"type":"text","value":", pass a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taskStore"},{"type":"text","value":" that those instances share."}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"get"},{"type":"text","value":": read one task by id."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":": save one task."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"delete"},{"type":"text","value":": remove one task."}]}]}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Tasks are part of spec "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2025-11-25"},{"type":"text","value":". Spec "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026-07-28"},{"type":"text","value":" has no tasks yet."}]},{"type":"table","align":[null,null],"header":[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Spec"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"What the call returns"}]}],"rows":[[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2025-11-25"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A task handle. The host polls "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/get"},{"type":"text","value":", then reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/result"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],[{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"2026-07-28"}]},{"type":"tableCell","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The tool result. The tool runs inline, and the call waits for it."}]}]]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On spec 2025, the server sets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"execution.taskSupport"},{"type":"text","value":" to "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"required"},{"type":"text","value":", and advertises the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks"},{"type":"text","value":" capability for "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tools/call"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"heading","depth":2,"id":"read-the-result","children":[{"type":"text","value":"Read the result"}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"On spec 2025, the call response is the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"CreateTaskResult"},{"type":"text","value":" from the spec. The "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"task"},{"type":"text","value":" field is a "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Task"},{"type":"text","value":" with status "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"working"},{"type":"text","value":". This status means that the tool function is still at work."}]},{"type":"code","value":"{\n  \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"task-id\" }],\n  \"task\": {\n    \"taskId\": \"task-id\",\n    \"status\": \"working\",\n    \"ttl\": null,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"lastUpdatedAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\"\n  }\n}","lang":"json"},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/get"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the same "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Task"},{"type":"text","value":" fields:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"taskId"},{"type":"text","value":": the id from the call."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"status"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"working"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completed"},{"type":"text","value":", or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"failed"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"ttl"},{"type":"text","value":": "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"null"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"createdAt"},{"type":"text","value":": the time of the first "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"lastUpdatedAt"},{"type":"text","value":": the time of the last "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"set"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"statusMessage"},{"type":"text","value":": the error text, when the status is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"failed"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/result"},{"type":"text","value":" wraps the value as "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"content"},{"type":"text","value":". When the value is an object, "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/result"},{"type":"text","value":" also returns "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredContent"},{"type":"text","value":". If the status is not "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completed"},{"type":"text","value":", "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/result"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the error "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Task result is not ready"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"A task uses one status:"}]},{"type":"list","ordered":false,"items":[{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"working"},{"type":"text","value":": the tool function is still at work."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completed"},{"type":"text","value":": the store holds the tool result."}]}]},{"type":"listItem","children":[{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"inlineCode","value":"failed"},{"type":"text","value":": the tool function threw an error."}]}]}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"If the tool function throws, the task keeps the text from that error in "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"statusMessage"},{"type":"text","value":". If that error has no text, the task keeps "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"The tool failed."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"An unknown task id on "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"tasks/get"},{"type":"text","value":" returns the error "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Task not found"},{"type":"text","value":". When the server has "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"auth"},{"type":"text","value":", a task belongs to the caller that started it: the "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"clientId"},{"type":"text","value":" of the token plus its "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"sub"},{"type":"text","value":" claim. Another caller also gets "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"Task not found"},{"type":"text","value":". "},{"type":"link","href":"./server-auth","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Auth"}]},{"type":"text","value":" shows how the verifier sets them."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"The host polls until the status is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completed"},{"type":"text","value":" or "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"failed"},{"type":"text","value":". A TanStack AI host polls until the task ends."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"See "},{"type":"link","href":"../tools/mcp","children":[{"type":"text","value":"MCP Server Tools"}]},{"type":"text","value":"."}]},{"type":"paragraph","children":[{"type":"text","value":"After the status is "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"completed"},{"type":"text","value":", the host reads "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"{ text: 'Quarterly report' }"},{"type":"text","value":" from "},{"type":"inlineCode","value":"structuredContent"},{"type":"text","value":"."}]}],"headings":[{"id":"what-a-task-tool-can-use","text":"What a task tool can use","level":2},{"id":"keep-the-worker-alive","text":"Keep the Worker alive","level":2},{"id":"keep-the-task-record","text":"Keep the task record","level":2},{"id":"spec-2025-and-spec-2026","text":"Spec 2025 and spec 2026","level":2},{"id":"read-the-result","text":"Read the result","level":2}]},"frameworks":[],"downloadMarkdown":"\nYour long tool holds the HTTP call until the work ends. You have no task id for the host to poll.\n\nSet `execution: 'task'` on `toolDefinition`.\n\nThe handler returns a task handle before the work ends. The tool function continues in this process. There is no queue.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer, inMemoryTaskStore } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst taskStore = inMemoryTaskStore()\n\nconst buildReport = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'build_report',\n  description: 'Build a long report',\n  execution: 'task',\n}).server(async () => {\n  const text = await writeReport()\n  return { text }\n})\n\nasync function writeReport() {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 5000)\n  })\n  return 'Quarterly report'\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(\n    request: Request,\n    _env: unknown,\n    ctx: { waitUntil(promise: Promise<unknown>): void },\n  ) {\n    const server = createMCPServer({\n      name: 'reports',\n      version: '1.0.0',\n      tools: [buildReport],\n      taskStore,\n      waitUntil: (promise) => ctx.waitUntil(promise),\n    })\n    return server.fetch(request)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nYour tool function returns the final value. When the tool function ends, the store saves that value.\n\n## What a task tool can use\n\nThe task keeps running after the call returns the task handle. So the task does not use the request that started it.\n\n- `ctx.context.requestInput` throws an error. Ask for input in a tool without `execution: 'task'`.\n- `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` option of `createMCPServer`. If you do not pass `sample`, `ctx.context.sample` throws an error.\n- `ctx.abortSignal` does not abort when the call request ends.\n\n## Keep the Worker alive\n\nIf you run on a Worker, pass `waitUntil` from the Worker context.\n\nThe server calls `waitUntil` with the tool promise. After the store saves the tool result or the tool error, this promise settles.\n\nIf you omit `waitUntil`, a Worker can stop before the tool function ends. On one long-lived process, you can omit `waitUntil`.\n\n## Keep the task record\n\n1. Create the store with `inMemoryTaskStore` outside `fetch`.\n2. Pass this store as `taskStore`.\n\nA new store on each request has no record of the old task.\n\nThe package `@tanstack/ai-mcp/server` exports `inMemoryTaskStore`. The default store keeps each task in memory for this process. If you build the server once, you can omit `taskStore`.\n\nIf more than one instance can receive `tasks/get`, pass a `taskStore` that those instances share.\n\n- `get`: read one task by id.\n- `set`: save one task.\n- `delete`: remove one task.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\nTasks are part of spec `2025-11-25`. Spec `2026-07-28` has no tasks yet.\n\n| Spec | What the call returns |\n| --- | --- |\n| `2025-11-25` | A task handle. The host polls `tasks/get`, then reads `tasks/result`. |\n| `2026-07-28` | The tool result. The tool runs inline, and the call waits for it. |\n\nOn spec 2025, the server sets `execution.taskSupport` to `required`, and advertises the `tasks` capability for `tools/call`.\n\n## Read the result\n\nOn spec 2025, the call response is the `CreateTaskResult` from the spec. The `task` field is a `Task` with status `working`. This status means that the tool function is still at work.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"task-id\" }],\n  \"task\": {\n    \"taskId\": \"task-id\",\n    \"status\": \"working\",\n    \"ttl\": null,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"lastUpdatedAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`tasks/get` returns the same `Task` fields:\n\n- `taskId`: the id from the call.\n- `status`: `working`, `completed`, or `failed`.\n- `ttl`: `null`.\n- `createdAt`: the time of the first `set`.\n- `lastUpdatedAt`: the time of the last `set`.\n- `statusMessage`: the error text, when the status is `failed`.\n\n`tasks/result` wraps the value as `content`. When the value is an object, `tasks/result` also returns `structuredContent`. If the status is not `completed`, `tasks/result` returns the error `Task result is not ready`.\n\nA task uses one status:\n\n- `working`: the tool function is still at work.\n- `completed`: the store holds the tool result.\n- `failed`: the tool function threw an error.\n\nIf the tool function throws, the task keeps the text from that error in `statusMessage`. If that error has no text, the task keeps `The tool failed.`\n\nAn unknown task id on `tasks/get` returns the error `Task not found`. When the server has `auth`, a task belongs to the caller that started it: the `clientId` of the token plus its `sub` claim. Another caller also gets `Task not found`. [MCP Server Auth](./server-auth) shows how the verifier sets them.\n\nThe host polls until the status is `completed` or `failed`. A TanStack AI host polls until the task ends.\n\nSee [MCP Server Tools](../tools/mcp).\n\nAfter the status is `completed`, the host reads `{ text: 'Quarterly report' }` from `structuredContent`.\n","originalRawMarkdown":"---\ntitle: MCP Server Tasks\nid: server-tasks\norder: 13\ndescription: \"A long MCP tool returns a task handle so the host can poll for the result.\"\nkeywords:\n  - tanstack ai\n  - mcp\n  - model context protocol\n  - mcp server\n  - execution\n  - task handle\n  - createMCPServer\n  - inMemoryTaskStore\n  - waitUntil\n---\n\nYour long tool holds the HTTP call until the work ends. You have no task id for the host to poll.\n\nSet `execution: 'task'` on `toolDefinition`.\n\nThe handler returns a task handle before the work ends. The tool function continues in this process. There is no queue.\n\n```ts\nimport { toolDefinition } from '@tanstack/ai'\nimport { createMCPServer, inMemoryTaskStore } from '@tanstack/ai-mcp/server'\n\nconst taskStore = inMemoryTaskStore()\n\nconst buildReport = toolDefinition({\n  name: 'build_report',\n  description: 'Build a long report',\n  execution: 'task',\n}).server(async () => {\n  const text = await writeReport()\n  return { text }\n})\n\nasync function writeReport() {\n  await new Promise((resolve) => {\n    setTimeout(resolve, 5000)\n  })\n  return 'Quarterly report'\n}\n\nexport default {\n  async fetch(\n    request: Request,\n    _env: unknown,\n    ctx: { waitUntil(promise: Promise<unknown>): void },\n  ) {\n    const server = createMCPServer({\n      name: 'reports',\n      version: '1.0.0',\n      tools: [buildReport],\n      taskStore,\n      waitUntil: (promise) => ctx.waitUntil(promise),\n    })\n    return server.fetch(request)\n  },\n}\n```\n\nYour tool function returns the final value. When the tool function ends, the store saves that value.\n\n## What a task tool can use\n\nThe task keeps running after the call returns the task handle. So the task does not use the request that started it.\n\n- `ctx.context.requestInput` throws an error. Ask for input in a tool without `execution: 'task'`.\n- `ctx.context.sample` calls the `sample` option of `createMCPServer`. If you do not pass `sample`, `ctx.context.sample` throws an error.\n- `ctx.abortSignal` does not abort when the call request ends.\n\n## Keep the Worker alive\n\nIf you run on a Worker, pass `waitUntil` from the Worker context.\n\nThe server calls `waitUntil` with the tool promise. After the store saves the tool result or the tool error, this promise settles.\n\nIf you omit `waitUntil`, a Worker can stop before the tool function ends. On one long-lived process, you can omit `waitUntil`.\n\n## Keep the task record\n\n1. Create the store with `inMemoryTaskStore` outside `fetch`.\n2. Pass this store as `taskStore`.\n\nA new store on each request has no record of the old task.\n\nThe package `@tanstack/ai-mcp/server` exports `inMemoryTaskStore`. The default store keeps each task in memory for this process. If you build the server once, you can omit `taskStore`.\n\nIf more than one instance can receive `tasks/get`, pass a `taskStore` that those instances share.\n\n- `get`: read one task by id.\n- `set`: save one task.\n- `delete`: remove one task.\n\n## Spec 2025 and spec 2026\n\nTasks are part of spec `2025-11-25`. Spec `2026-07-28` has no tasks yet.\n\n| Spec | What the call returns |\n| --- | --- |\n| `2025-11-25` | A task handle. The host polls `tasks/get`, then reads `tasks/result`. |\n| `2026-07-28` | The tool result. The tool runs inline, and the call waits for it. |\n\nOn spec 2025, the server sets `execution.taskSupport` to `required`, and advertises the `tasks` capability for `tools/call`.\n\n## Read the result\n\nOn spec 2025, the call response is the `CreateTaskResult` from the spec. The `task` field is a `Task` with status `working`. This status means that the tool function is still at work.\n\n```json\n{\n  \"content\": [{ \"type\": \"text\", \"text\": \"task-id\" }],\n  \"task\": {\n    \"taskId\": \"task-id\",\n    \"status\": \"working\",\n    \"ttl\": null,\n    \"createdAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\",\n    \"lastUpdatedAt\": \"2026-09-22T12:00:00.000Z\"\n  }\n}\n```\n\n`tasks/get` returns the same `Task` fields:\n\n- `taskId`: the id from the call.\n- `status`: `working`, `completed`, or `failed`.\n- `ttl`: `null`.\n- `createdAt`: the time of the first `set`.\n- `lastUpdatedAt`: the time of the last `set`.\n- `statusMessage`: the error text, when the status is `failed`.\n\n`tasks/result` wraps the value as `content`. When the value is an object, `tasks/result` also returns `structuredContent`. If the status is not `completed`, `tasks/result` returns the error `Task result is not ready`.\n\nA task uses one status:\n\n- `working`: the tool function is still at work.\n- `completed`: the store holds the tool result.\n- `failed`: the tool function threw an error.\n\nIf the tool function throws, the task keeps the text from that error in `statusMessage`. If that error has no text, the task keeps `The tool failed.`\n\nAn unknown task id on `tasks/get` returns the error `Task not found`. When the server has `auth`, a task belongs to the caller that started it: the `clientId` of the token plus its `sub` claim. Another caller also gets `Task not found`. [MCP Server Auth](./server-auth) shows how the verifier sets them.\n\nThe host polls until the status is `completed` or `failed`. A TanStack AI host polls until the task ends.\n\nSee [MCP Server Tools](../tools/mcp).\n\nAfter the status is `completed`, the host reads `{ text: 'Quarterly report' }` from `structuredContent`.\n"}
